    "body": "## Motivation\n\nCloses #30428.\n\nWhen the SGLang inference server runs with parameter offloading enabled, it uses `HostSharedMemoryManager` to allocate shared memory blocks and registers them with CUDA. However, `HostSharedMemoryManager` lacks a teardown implementation, leaving CUDA host pointer registrations leaked and POSIX shared memory segments dangling in `/dev/shm` after the server terminates.\n\nThis PR implements the missing teardown lifecycle logic to ensure resources are cleanly reclaimed.\n\n## Modifications\n\n1. **`HostSharedMemoryManager` dispose logic**:\n   - Implemented `dispose()` method in `HostSharedMemoryManager` inside `python/sglang/srt/utils/host_shared_memory.py`.\n   - Iterates through allocated shared memory records to unregister them via `cudaHostUnregister` and close/unlink (`shm.unlink()` on rank 0) the shared memory segments.\n   - Added global `dispose_host_shared_memory_manager()` helper.\n2. **Teardown integration**:\n   - Modified `release_host_resources()` in `Scheduler` inside `python/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py` to invoke `dispose_host_shared_memory_manager()`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nN/A. This is a lifecycle/teardown cleanup change and does not affect model outputs.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A. Teardown logic only runs at shutdown time.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #30211616404](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/30211616404)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #30211616287](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/30211616287)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
